<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>armless: arm64 Linux in a browser tab</title>
<meta name="description" content="armless is an AArch64 machine emulator written in Rust. It boots unmodified arm64 Linux in a browser tab through WebAssembly, and natively through a Rust crate.">
<meta property="og:title" content="armless: arm64 Linux in a browser tab">
<meta property="og:description" content="An AArch64 machine emulator written in Rust. The whole machine, devices included, is Rust.">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:site_name" content="armless">
<meta property="og:url" content="<%= @site %>">
<meta property="og:image" content="<%= @site %>og.png">
<meta property="og:image:type" content="image/png">
<meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
<meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
<meta property="og:image:alt" content="armless: arm64 Linux, in a browser tab. Beside the headline, the Mandelbrot set as the page's machine draws it in its console.">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="dark">
<link rel="icon" href="favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="preload" href="fonts/SpaceMono-400.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
<script src="site.js" defer></script>
<%= if @demo? do %><link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/xterm.css">
<script src="demo.js" defer></script><% end %>
</head>
<body class="landing">
<a class="skip" href="#machine">Skip to the machine</a>

<header class="bar">
  <a class="name" href="index.html">armless</a>
  <nav aria-label="Site"><a href="docs/index.html">docs</a> <a href="<%= @repo %>/releases">releases</a> <a href="<%= @repo %>">source</a></nav>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>arm64 Linux,<br>in a browser tab.</h1>
    <p class="sub">An AArch64 machine emulator written in Rust. The whole machine, devices included, is Rust.</p>
    <p class="actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="docs/getting-started.html">Read the docs</a> <a class="btn" href="<%= @repo %>/releases">Releases</a></p>
  </section>

  <section class="machine" id="machine" aria-label="A machine running in this tab">
    <div class="pane pane-console">
      <div class="pane-bar"><span class="pane-name">/bin/sh</span>
        <span id="keys" class="keys" hidden>
          <button type="button" class="btn" data-send="\x03" aria-label="Send ctrl+c">^C</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn" data-send="nproc\n">nproc</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn" data-send="cat /proc/cpuinfo\n">cpuinfo</button>
        </span>
        <span class="end"><span id="status" role="status" data-state="off"><%= if @demo?, do: "needs JavaScript", else: "not in this build" %></span></span>
      </div>
      <div class="console">
        <div id="terminal" role="group" aria-label="The machine's console. Ctrl+c stops the drawing. Escape, then Tab, leaves the console."></div>
        <p id="console-log" class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <p id="console-fallback" class="fallback" <%= if @demo?, do: "hidden" %>><%= if @demo?, do: "", else: "The machine is not part of this build." %></p>
        <noscript><p class="fallback">The machine needs JavaScript and WebAssembly.</p></noscript>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="pane pane-memory">
      <div class="pane-bar"><span class="pane-name">machine</span><span class="pane-note">vm.smp_report()</span></div>
      <div class="memory">
        <dl class="figures">
          <div class="wide"><dt>instructions per second, all CPUs</dt><dd><span id="m-mips">-</span><small>MIPS</small></dd></div>
          <div><dt>CPUs</dt><dd id="m-cpus">-</dd><dd class="note" id="m-cores"></dd></div>
          <div><dt>JIT blocks</dt><dd id="m-jit">-</dd></div>
          <div><dt>linear memory</dt><dd><span id="m-linear">-</span><small>MiB</small></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <ul class="cpus" id="cpus" aria-label="Instructions per second, each CPU"></ul>
        <figure class="chart">
          <svg id="chart" viewBox="0 0 520 200" role="img" aria-label="Instructions per second across all CPUs, over the last two minutes"></svg>
          <figcaption><span class="key live"></span>all CPUs</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <p class="caption">Linux 6.8, booted in this tab from an initramfs with busybox, with as many CPUs as this device can spare. One awk per CPU draws a trench run, a new one every time. Ctrl+c stops it. Escape, then Tab, leaves the console.<span id="one-cpu" hidden> This browser could not isolate the page, so the machine has one CPU.</span></p>

  <section class="embed" id="embed" aria-labelledby="embed-h">
    <h2 id="embed-h">Embed it</h2>
    <pre tabindex="0"><code><%= @embed %></code></pre>
    <p><a href="docs/browser-api.html">Every option, event and call</a></p>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="foot">
  <span>armless <%= @version %>. BSD 2-Clause. <a href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/snowglobe">snowglobe</a> uses it.</span>
  <nav aria-label="Footer"><a href="docs/index.html">docs</a> <a href="<%= @repo %>/releases">releases</a> <a href="<%= @repo %>">source</a></nav>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
